    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "DNG are delighted to present this truly exceptional red brick, double bay windowed period home to the market, superbly positioned on this highly sought-after residential road in the heart of Rathgar, Dublin 6. Extending to approximately 235 sq.m. including the converted attic (approximately 200 sq.m. excluding the attic), this impressive home offers a wonderful combination of elegant period proportions, beautifully considered interiors and excellent family living space. Presented in excellent condition throughout, the house has been finished with considerable style and is ready for its new owners to simply move in and enjoy.\n\nA long and welcoming entrance hallway leads to two superbly appointed reception rooms, while to the rear the extended kitchen and dining area is undoubtedly the heart of the home. Generous in scale and flooded with natural light, this is a wonderful space for both everyday family life and entertaining. A useful utility room and guest WC complete the ground floor accommodation.\n\nUpstairs, the accommodation is arranged over the first floor and two return levels comprising three bedrooms together with a family bathroom. Originally arranged as four bedrooms, the current owners have cleverly incorporated one of the double bedrooms into the principal suite to create a particularly luxurious en-suite bathroom serving the main front bedroom. This generous space could also be readily converted back to a fourth bedroom if desired, giving future owners excellent flexibility as their needs evolve. The converted attic adds further superb accommodation, comprising a large and versatile room with excellent ceiling height together with its bathroom. \n\nThe owners' eye for design is evident throughout the property, with stylish finishes complementing the wonderful proportions and character of the original house. A strong C BER rating is another significant advantage, adding to the overall appeal of this very special home.\n\nOutside, the property is approached through an attractive railed front garden, while to the rear lies a superb south-west-facing garden extending to approximately 55 ft. - an enviable feature and an ideal setting in which to enjoy the afternoon and evening sun. Rear access provides additional convenience and offers potential to create off-street parking, while on-street permit parking is available to the front.\n\nThe location is difficult to beat: Upper Rathmines Road is within a two-minute walk and offers an excellent selection of local amenities including Grocer on the Green, Tesco Express, Lawlor's and Connolly's Fish. The villages of Rathmines, Rathgar and Ranelagh are also all within a short walk, placing an outstanding choice of shops, cafés, restaurants and amenities close at hand. Dublin city centre is within walking distance and is also easily accessed by regular bus services and the Luas. \n\nSubstantial, stylish and superbly located, this is an outstanding Dublin 6 home with all the ingredients for modern family living."
      },
