        "Content": "<ul><li> Handsome red brick, double bay windowed period home</li><li> Highly sought-after Rathgar location</li><li> Approx. 235 sq.m (c. 200 sq.m excluding the attic)</li><li> Presented in excellent condition throughout</li><li> Beautiful red brick façade recently sanded and re-pointed</li><li> Stylish and beautifully appointed interiors</li><li> Two elegant reception rooms</li><li> Superb extended kitchen and dining space</li><li> Separate utility room and ground floor guest WC</li><li> Luxurious principal bedroom suite</li><li> Three bedrooms arranged over the first floor and two return levels</li><li> Luxurious en-suite easily converted back to a fourth bedroom if desired</li><li> Family bathroom</li><li> Spacious converted attic room with own bathroom</li><li> Strong C BER rating</li><li> Approx. 55 ft. south-west-facing rear garden</li><li> Rear access with potential to create off-street parking</li><li> Attractive railed front garden</li><li> On-street permit parking</li><li> Upper Rathmines Road within a two-minute walk</li><li> Rathmines, Rathgar and Ranelagh villages close by</li><li> Close to range of well-regarded primary and secondary schools</li><li> Dublin city centre within walking distance</li><li> Excellent bus services and Luas stop nearby</li><li> Superb turnkey family home</li></ul>"
